host/anyhost.cpp: minimal Linux host of the AnyPS5 layer, mirroring the
Win32 launcher flow (wWinMain @ 757692f6): CLI (--game-dir/--version/
--help), real SDL2 init (VIDEO|GAMECONTROLLER) with forced dummy-driver
retry for headless/CI/Android, greppable markers (SOS_HOST_STARTED,
SOS_HOST_SDL2_OK, SOS_HOST_MISSING_GAME_FILES, SOS_HOST_VALIDATE_OK,
SOS_HOST_SDL2_FAIL, SOS_HOST_INTERNAL_ERROR), strict validation order
(eboot.bin/eboot.elf -> ELF magic -> sce_sys -> Media -> libs ->
tools/relinker), PT-BR user messages equivalent to the Win32 texts,
SDL_ShowSimpleMessageBox only when a real video driver is active,
exit 1 for missing files / 2 for internal errors, no abort()/signals.
Post-validation path (relink + exec of sos_runtime with logs, app0
symlinks) is present and guarded by SOS_HOST_RELINK_START; not
exercised in M2 (requires a game dump).

host/CMakeLists.txt: standalone superproject (no root CMakeLists
changes) building SDL2 static minimal dummy-first (X11/Wayland/KMSDRM/
OpenGL/GLES/Vulkan/Render off; Joystick/Haptic/Hidapi on; STATIC_PIC on)
and core/relinker statically via the root CMakeLists linker-flag
save/clear/restore pattern; anyhost linked to SDL2-static with
-static -static-libgcc -static-libstdc++; BUILD_TESTING off.

Evidence: both binaries build as 'ELF 64-bit LSB executable, x86-64,
statically linked' (gcc 14.2, CMake 4.4.4, Ninja); smokes exercise all
missing-file reasons plus relinker usage exit.
